<title>MEXICO: Mexico's Pemex reports April average crude exports.</title>
<headline>Mexico's Pemex reports April average crude exports.</headline>
<dateline>MEXICO CITY 1997-05-27</dateline>
<text>
<p>Mexico's state oil and gas monopoly Petroleos Mexicanos (Pemex) said Tuesday it exported an average 1.817 million barrels per day (bpd) of crude in April..</p>
<p>This figure is the company's highest crude export level in at least five years, according to the Pemex report. Last April Pemex exported an average 1.561 million bpd.</p>
<p>The following is a breakdown of crudes by type and destination in average bpd for the month:</p>
<p>    Maya exports			  1,042,000 bpd</p>
<p>    Isthmus exports			 254,000 bpd</p>
<p>    Olmeca exports			  520,000 bpd</p>
<p>Geographical Distribution</p>
<p>    North America			 1,562,000 bpd</p>
<p>    Europe				    194,000 bpd</p>
<p>    Far East				   61,000 bpd</p>
<p>((--Timna Tanners, Mexico City newsroom +525 728-7903. E-mail at timna.tanners@reuters.com))</p>
</text>
